-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Army Moves
  Publisher   Imagine / Dinamic, 1987
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Army Moves (1987)(Imagine)(128K)[re-release].z80
  MD5         9c14e2564e3f9956ff6ff973dac77537

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures are drawn on the Next's own graphics layers, so they keep their
  own colours and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is
  unchanged.

  Pace        original (-0.61% measured in JNext 1.1.104, against the original
              .z80 on a 128K machine, game state in lockstep)

  Changes     1.0: figures in their own colours on a double-buffered Layer 2,
              in the game's own plot order, over the original bitmap; scenery
              in its own attributes; both parts; the plot, restore and copy
              run whole at 28 MHz in pace windows; the original loading
              screen; Sinclair's 48K ROM as the whole alt ROM (NextZXOS 26.11
              safe); the game's speed restored after every hook; two tested
              cheats

  Note        Keys: on the game's menu 1 keys (redefine), 2 joystick, 3 play,
              4 part 2, M music on or off; part 2 asks for the access code the
              game gives at the end of part 1. The original look: figures keep
              their own colours and the scenery keeps its own. In the original
              the jeep turned red over the bridge and painted cells of the
              jungle in the soldier's colour; here each figure's ink is drawn
              on Layer 2, in the game's own order, over the original bitmap.
              The 128K release, both parts, with its AY music. Fits a 1MB
              Next. Known issues: in part 2 small items and bullets the game
              leaves to the cell's ink still take it, as in the original; part
              1 figures with no colour of their own are drawn in the sky's
              ink; in JNext it runs 0.6 to 1.2 percent faster than the
              original over whole runs, the slowest 20-update stretch +0.31
              percent; an occasional interrupt was lost in part 2 (up to 3 in
              about 2,700 frames) where the original lost none. Missing: no
              Enhanced colour set yet; natural play to the end; hardware
              untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Immunity

  The archive's POKEs for this 128K release, part 1, each tested alone in the
  simulator, same keys with and without it: Infinite lives (lives never fall),
  Immunity (lives never fall). Left out: Jeep doesn't fall and No enemies (no
  clear result in testing).

